WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.884 --> 00:00:21.376
At the sound of the maid's scream, Kathleen ran into Gerald's room.

2
00:00:21.396 --> 00:00:22.897
"What's wrong?"

3
00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:25.539
"One minute Gerald was gone!"

4
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:26.880
said Eliza.

5
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.782
"The next minute he was in the bed!

6
00:00:29.802 --> 00:00:32.084
I don't know what's wrong with me.

7
00:00:32.912 --> 00:00:35.833
Yesterday I was hearing voices, and now this."

8
00:00:37.314 --> 00:00:39.475
Eliza shook her head as she left the room.

9
00:00:43.957 --> 00:00:46.258
happened?" Kathleen asked Gerald.

10
00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:50.400
"The ring came off when Eliza called me.

11
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:51.800
I'm hungry.

12
00:00:52.481 --> 00:00:53.761
I'll tell you everything later."

13
00:00:56.662 --> 00:00:59.824
After breakfast Gerald remembered he'd left the ring in bed.

14
00:01:02.112 --> 00:01:05.575
But when he went upstairs, Eliza had already made his bed.

15
00:01:07.736 --> 00:01:08.897
He asked her about the ring.

16
00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:12.760
"I didn't see anything," she said.

17
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.303
"If there was a ring in the bed, I'd have seen it."

18
00:01:19.425 --> 00:01:23.548
The children searched every corner of the room, but couldn't find the ring.

19
00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.632
Soon they gave up because they had to meet Mabel in town.

20
00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.134
They sat on a wall to wait for her.

21
00:01:34.154 --> 00:01:39.858
"Hey, you went back to normal faster than I did," Mabel said to Gerald.

22
00:01:44.442 --> 00:01:47.204
Now Gerald could tell the story of the three burglars.

23
00:01:49.926 --> 00:01:53.970
After throwing the rock, he'd returned to the room where they were loading their sacks.

24
00:01:57.552 --> 00:02:01.696
He'd followed the men out into the night and discovered their hiding place.

25
00:02:04.788 --> 00:02:07.869
"Look, there's Officer Johnson," said Gerald.

26
00:02:07.889 --> 00:02:09.790
"I need to talk to him."

27
00:02:13.071 --> 00:02:16.273
Gerald hopped off the wall and went over to Officer Johnson.

28
00:02:18.914 --> 00:02:21.935
"Would you like to catch those burglars who've been stealing silver?"

29
00:02:21.955 --> 00:02:25.236
"What do you know about that?"

30
00:02:25.777 --> 00:02:27.177
Johnson asked suspiciously.

31
00:02:27.197 --> 00:02:32.119
"I saw something last night, but I could get in trouble for being out late.

32
00:02:32.439 --> 00:02:34.140
Do you promise not to tell anyone?"

33
00:02:34.616 --> 00:02:35.457
Johnson nodded.

34
00:02:35.477 --> 00:02:39.320
"I saw three men taking silver from the castle.

35
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.621
I know where they put it."

36
00:02:40.641 --> 00:02:42.663
"So you wrote the note?"

37
00:02:43.223 --> 00:02:44.404
Johnson said eagerly.

38
00:02:44.424 --> 00:02:51.850
"Yes." Gerald explained how he'd watched the men go down to the river.

39
00:02:52.751 --> 00:02:55.233
They had tied their bags of silver under a dock.

40
00:02:57.174 --> 00:03:01.718
Tonight, after dark, they planned to retrieve the silver and escape by boat.

41
00:03:02.719 --> 00:03:05.133
"You can catch them then," said Gerald.

42
00:03:05.153 --> 00:03:07.755
"But which dock is their hiding spot?"

43
00:03:08.195 --> 00:03:08.975
asked Johnson.

44
00:03:08.995 --> 00:03:12.718
"Follow me," said Gerald.

45
00:03:12.738 --> 00:03:19.703
"When I take out my handkerchief and blow my nose, that'll be the place."

46
00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:22.585
Gerald went back to the other children.

47
00:03:22.605 --> 00:03:25.607
"Come on!

48
00:03:26.008 --> 00:03:27.289
Let's play follow-the-leader."

49
00:03:30.311 --> 00:03:34.725
The children followed him, running and jumping and imitating his every step.

50
00:03:35.785 --> 00:03:37.406
Johnson followed at a distance.

51
00:03:41.807 --> 00:03:45.048
On one dock Gerald suddenly stopped and blew his nose.

52
00:03:46.508 --> 00:03:48.629
Then he led the children back to the school.

53
00:03:56.391 --> 00:04:01.092
brought our friend Mabel home for lunch," said Kathleen when Eliza opened the door.

54
00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.520
"Where's Mademoiselle?"

55
00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:06.161
"She's gone to visit the castle.

56
00:04:06.561 --> 00:04:08.522
The grounds are open to the public today.

57
00:04:08.922 --> 00:04:10.242
Now hurry up with your lunch.

58
00:04:10.763 --> 00:04:12.083
This is my afternoon off.

59
00:04:12.743 --> 00:04:14.724
My fiancé doesn't like waiting for me."

60
00:04:21.386 --> 00:04:23.566
The children ate quickly and Eliza left.

61
00:04:23.586 --> 00:04:25.327
"Where's the ring?"

62
00:04:25.827 --> 00:04:26.427
asked Mabel.

63
00:04:26.447 --> 00:04:29.608
"I really need to put it back."

64
00:04:30.692 --> 00:04:33.313
"I haven't had a turn yet," protested Jimmy.

65
00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:38.154
"When we find it—" "When you find it?"

66
00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:39.394
said Mabel.

67
00:04:40.275 --> 00:04:42.035
They told her about losing the ring.

68
00:04:42.055 --> 00:04:45.796
"Oh no!"

69
00:04:46.376 --> 00:04:47.157
cried Mabel.

70
00:04:47.177 --> 00:04:49.417
"We have to find it!"

71
00:04:51.198 --> 00:04:55.919
The children searched and searched Gerald's room, but they still couldn't find the ring.

72
00:04:57.019 --> 00:04:59.420
Suddenly there was pounding at the back door.

73
00:05:01.312 --> 00:05:02.832
Kathleen ran downstairs.

74
00:05:03.753 --> 00:05:05.933
A strange man stood near the doorstep.

75
00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:11.495
His eyes were open wide with amazement.

76
00:05:12.535 --> 00:05:14.316
One arm was stretched out toward the door.

77
00:05:15.216 --> 00:05:18.277
The rest of him looked as if he were trying to run the other way.

78
00:05:18.297 --> 00:05:20.658
"Let go of me!"

79
00:05:21.138 --> 00:05:21.698
he cried.

80
00:05:21.718 --> 00:05:23.959
"I won't let go of you!"

81
00:05:24.499 --> 00:05:25.639
said Eliza's voice.

82
00:05:26.579 --> 00:05:28.560
But no Eliza could be seen.
